  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the goal is to establish a strong, well-motivated multimodal baseline that reduces uncertainty about the core design space. config_004 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) uses two well-established encoders (scVI for scRNA-seq, ResNet50 for images) combined with a principled multi-profile aggregation (transformer) and a simple, interpretable fusion (weighted). This configuration sits near the 'center of mass' of the design space: it is complex enough to be competitive but relies on robust, validated components so that any failure signals a structural issue rather than an encoder choice. Performance here gives a strong reference point: if it is competitive, subsequent experiments can explore scgpt/ViT-L upgrades and alternative fusion; if it underperforms, I can ablate to identify whether multiprofile+transformer or the specific encoder pair is the bottleneck. With 9 experiments remaining, this single informative anchor maximally guides the next 9 choices."
}

